[{"id":2606736514,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6bX6SC","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_tilemap_large.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18738578/test_tilemap_large.zip)\r\n\r\n### Physics seams issues\r\n\r\n*Holding left arrow in the testing project's main scene.*\r\n\r\n### Before\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8ac8688c-1f3d-41a5-a8bf-8578610eb2f4\r\n\r\n### After\r\n\r\n*Physics seams issues still occur occasionally, but are much rarer and less severe.*\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/69dff3a4-3957-463e-a61b-fe4c1a0bb547\r\n\r\n### After (physics quadrant size set to `2**31 - 1`)\r\n\r\n*This fully avoids the issue, but makes editing slower in the editor and may have adverse performance issues in large scenes (due to each object having to check collision against the entire level's shape).*\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e8d0f8ca-fae6-4c0d-b423-75c89b6bc0a1\r\n\r\n### Performance\r\n\r\n<details open>\r\n\r\n<summary>PC specifications</summary>\r\n\r\n- **CPU:** Intel Core i9-13900K\r\n- **GPU:** NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090\r\n- **RAM:** 64 GB (2×32 GB DDR5-5800 C30)\r\n- **SSD:** Solidigm P44 Pro 2 TB\r\n- **OS:** Linux (Fedora 41)\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nCommand line used for testing (we render in a tiny window to avoid GPU bottlenecks[^1]):\r\n\r\n[^1]: `--disable-render-loop` breaks `--print-fps` reporting, so we can't use it to test physics performance.\r\n\r\n```\r\ngodot --path /path/to/project lots_of_tiles.tscn --resolution 64x64 --print-fps\r\n```\r\n\r\n1000 RigidBodies enclosed in a complex TileMap.\r\n\r\n### Before\r\n\r\n*We encounter a \"physics spiral of death\" phenomenon, hence the sudden decrease in FPS at some point.*\r\n\r\n```\r\nProject FPS: 391 (2.55 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 577 (1.73 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 11 (90.90 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 8 (125.00 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 60 (16.66 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 9 (111.11 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 20 (50.00 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 590 (1.69 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 328 (3.04 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 399 (2.50 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 442 (2.26 mspf)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### After\r\n\r\n*No more physics spiral of death, and overall performance is greatly improved.*\r\n\r\n```\r\nProject FPS: 837 (1.19 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 488 (2.04 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 698 (1.43 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 876 (1.14 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 900 (1.11 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 872 (1.14 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 880 (1.13 mspf)\r\nProject FPS: 649 (1.54 mspf)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Feedback\r\n\r\n- The property should be documented in the class reference, and it should have a property hint added to set a suitable range. I'd suggest something like `1,1024,1` as sizes above 1024 will likely run into the aforementioned performance issue, on top of being very slow for editing.\r\n- We could sidestep the editing performance problem at large quadrant sizes by clamping the size of the physics quadrant while in the editor to a value like 16 or 32.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102662#pullrequestreview-2606736514","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102662","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-02-10T17:58:19Z"},{"id":2607304871,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6baFCn","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?u=fc85633b469acb6e7baef4d